-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.19 תוספת תגבור הוראה
-- The "teaching reinforcement" supplement: its amount and how it is
-- updated, the share of the position it is paid on (with the principals'
-- separate rule), and what it counts for.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.19 תוספת תגבור הוראה`

@desc A teaching employee's month, as far as section 1.19 asks about it.
DECLARE `reinforcement month` HAS
    `month as a date`        IS A NUMBER  @desc the salary month as a number YYYYMMDD
    `position share held`    IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held (1 = one full position; 1.5 = 150%)
    `is a principal`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc the employee is a school principal
    `supplement for a full position` IS A NUMBER @desc the supplement's amount that month for one full position, as updated under paragraph 2 (an input: the update rates are set outside the takanon)

§§ `1.19 ¶2 The amount and its updating`

-- ¶2: the one amount the section prints, from 1.1.01; and how it moves.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_19__ssec_1_19/p2
`the amount from 1.1.01` MEANS 124.2
`1 January 2001` MEANS 20010101

DECLARE `kind of increase` IS ONE OF
    `cost-of-living increment`
    `general wage increase`

DECLARE `increase` HAS
    `kind of the increase` IS A `kind of increase`
    `rate of the increase` IS A NUMBER  @desc the rate, e.g. 0.02 for 2%; set by the agreements and the Treasury, never by this file

-- ¶2: while the collective agreement is in force the supplement moves at the
-- dates and rates of the cost-of-living increments only; after its term it
-- moves by the general wage increases when given AND by the cost-of-living
-- increments. Which agreement, and when its term ends, the text does not say
-- (F-1.19-a), so it is an input here.
GIVEN `during the agreement's term` IS A BOOLEAN, i IS AN `increase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the increase updates the supplement` `during the agreement's term` i IF
    CONSIDER i's `kind of the increase`
    WHEN `cost-of-living increment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `general wage increase`    THEN NOT `during the agreement's term`

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, `during the agreement's term` IS A BOOLEAN, i IS AN `increase`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement after one increase` amount `during the agreement's term` i IS
    IF `the increase updates the supplement` `during the agreement's term` i
    THEN amount TIMES (1 PLUS i's `rate of the increase`)
    ELSE amount

-- F-1.19-a: one general wage increase of 2% (a placeholder rate) moves the
-- 1.1.01 amount after the agreement's term and does not move it during it;
-- the text never says which agreement, or when its term ends.
`a 2% general wage increase` MEANS `increase` WITH
    `kind of the increase` IS `general wage increase`
    `rate of the increase` IS 0.02

`the updating rule turns on an agreement the section does not identify` MEANS
    NOT (`the supplement after one increase` `the amount from 1.1.01` TRUE  `a 2% general wage increase`
         EQUALS `the supplement after one increase` `the amount from 1.1.01` FALSE `a 2% general wage increase`)
#ASSERT `the updating rule turns on an agreement the section does not identify`

§§ `1.19 ¶3 The share of the position it is paid on`

-- ¶3: from 1.1.97 a teaching employee is paid on the whole position,
-- beyond one position too. Principals were left out of that decision and
-- "continued" on their position share up to one position; from 1.9.01 they
-- too are paid on the whole position, but not beyond 150%. Before 1.1.97
-- everyone is read as capped at one position: the principals "continued"
-- that rule, which is the only thing the section says about it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_19__ssec_1_19/p3
`1 January 1997`   MEANS 19970101
`1 September 2001` MEANS 20010901

GIVEN m IS A `reinforcement month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position share the supplement is paid on` m IS
    IF m's `is a principal`
    THEN IF m's `month as a date` AT LEAST `1 September 2001`
         THEN min (m's `position share held`) 1.5
         ELSE min (m's `position share held`) 1
    ELSE IF m's `month as a date` AT LEAST `1 January 1997`
         THEN m's `position share held`
         ELSE min (m's `position share held`) 1

@export default The monthly teaching-reinforcement supplement (tosefet tigbur hora'a) a teaching employee is owed under section 1.19 of the takanon
GIVEN m IS A `reinforcement month` @desc the employee's month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the reinforcement supplement` m IS
    m's `supplement for a full position` TIMES `the position share the supplement is paid on` m

§§ `1.19 ¶4–¶5 What the supplement counts for`

-- ¶4: it is the base of the percentage allowances and part of the salary for
-- the hourly value, social conditions, and the determining salary for
-- severance and pension. ¶5: it is NOT a component in the erosion check.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_19__ssec_1_19/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_19__ssec_1_19/p5
DECLARE `salary purpose` IS ONE OF
    `the base of the percentage allowances`
    `the hourly value`
    `social conditions`
    `the determining salary for severance pay`
    `the determining salary for pension`
    `the erosion check under section 8 of the agreement`

GIVEN p IS A `salary purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the erosion check under section 8 of the agreement` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ¶4, last words: the supplement appears on a separate line of the payslip,
-- each salary month.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_19__ssec_1_19/p4
DECLARE `payslip action` IS ONE OF
    `show the supplement on a separate payslip line`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `payslip action`
DECIDE `a separate payslip line` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `show the supplement on a separate payslip line`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.19: the supplement appears on a separate line of the payslip"

-- Worked examples. The full-position amount is the 1.1.01 figure the text
-- prints; the position shares are placeholders.
`a teacher at 120% in 2002` MEANS `reinforcement month` WITH
    `month as a date`                IS 20020301
    `position share held`            IS 1.2
    `is a principal`                 IS FALSE
    `supplement for a full position` IS `the amount from 1.1.01`

`a principal at 180% in 2002` MEANS `reinforcement month` WITH
    `month as a date`                IS 20020301
    `position share held`            IS 1.8
    `is a principal`                 IS TRUE
    `supplement for a full position` IS `the amount from 1.1.01`

`a principal at 120% in 1999` MEANS `reinforcement month` WITH
    `month as a date`                IS 19990301
    `position share held`            IS 1.2
    `is a principal`                 IS TRUE
    `supplement for a full position` IS `the amount from 1.1.01`

#ASSERT `the reinforcement supplement` `a teacher at 120% in 2002` EQUALS 124.2 TIMES 1.2
#ASSERT `the reinforcement supplement` `a principal at 180% in 2002` EQUALS 124.2 TIMES 1.5
#ASSERT `the reinforcement supplement` `a principal at 120% in 1999` EQUALS 124.2
#ASSERT NOT `the supplement counts for` `the erosion check under section 8 of the agreement`
#ASSERT `the supplement counts for` `the determining salary for pension`

`a cost-of-living increment of 1%` MEANS `increase` WITH
    `kind of the increase` IS `cost-of-living increment`
    `rate of the increase` IS 0.01
#EVAL `the supplement after one increase` `the amount from 1.1.01` TRUE `a cost-of-living increment of 1%`

#TRACE `a separate payslip line` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `show the supplement on a separate payslip line` AT 1

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_19__ssec_1_19/p1 An amendment note ("this section was updated on 21.7.02"); it carries no rule.
